# Invalid-placement feedback position and duration

Move invalid-placement messages lower on the screen and shorten their display period.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Road and building validation messages appear towards the bottom of the Board without covering bottom controls.
- [x] Each message remains visible for 1.5 seconds, then dismisses automatically.
- [x] A later invalid attempt replaces and restarts the active message deterministically.
- [x] Board editing and construction-plan placement use the same presentation behavior.
- [x] Existing exact validation copy remains unchanged.
- [x] Timing logic is cancellable and cannot dismiss a newer message early.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Verification

- Add deterministic state/timing coverage where possible and UI coverage for placement and automatic dismissal.

## Evidence

- Moved the shared Board placement message from the centre to 96 points above the viewport bottom so it remains low without overlapping the overlaid bottom bar.
- Shortened the cancellable dismissal task to 1,500 ms; every new error cancels and replaces the prior task before scheduling its own dismissal.
- Added UI regression coverage for lower-half positioning, automatic dismissal within two seconds, and remaining on the invalid placement screen.
- The complete app and test bundles compile using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks018-024-derived`.
